<li class="custom-item" id="07W5"><p>
 Let $\mathcal{F}$ be cofibered in groupoids over $\mathcal{C}$. For $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ set $\overline{\mathcal{F}}(U)$ equal to the set of isomorphisms classes of the category $\mathcal{F}(U)$. If $f : U \to V$ is a morphism of $\mathcal{C}$, then we obtain a map of sets $\overline{\mathcal{F}}(U) \to \overline{\mathcal{F}}(V)$ by mapping the isomorphism class of $x$ to the isomorphism class of a pushforward $f_*x$ of $x$ see (<a href="/tag/06SH" data-tag="06SH">4</a>). Then $\overline{\mathcal{F}} : \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ is a functor. Similarly, if $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ is a morphism of cofibered categories, we denote by $\overline{\varphi }: \overline{\mathcal{F}} \to \overline{\mathcal{G}}$ the associated morphism of functors. 
</p>
